    "external_precedent_not_adopted": {
      "definition_as_stated": "Adjusted Task Score = simple average of three normalized ratings (frequency, importance, relevance), each divided by its maximum (7, 5, 100); missing ratings imputed with the occupation mean; SOC-6 scores summed into SOC-4; Weighted Task Share = task's Adjusted Task Score / sum over the occupation's tasks, so shares sum to 1 per occupation.",
      "locator": "GDPval paper, Appendix 'Classifying Occupations as Digital', printed pp. 24-25, and footnotes 12-14",
      "onet_release_used_by_that_paper": "O*NET 28.3, with 29.0 for two occupations; NOT 26.1",
      "status": "RECORDED AS PRECEDENT ONLY. Not adopted, not implemented.",
      "unresolved_before_this_could_be_reused": [
        "The paper normalizes frequency by 'maximum frequency value is 7', implying a scalar 1-7 frequency rating. O*NET 26.1 has no such column: FT is a seven-row percentage distribution per occupation-task. Collapsing it to a scalar (modal category, expected category, or something else) is an unstated choice.",
        "Weighted Task Share is a share of RATING MASS, not of work time. Calling it a time-share would misname it."
      ],
      "what": "The GDPval paper builds a 'Weighted Task Share' from exactly these three ratings."
    },
